       These functions return an array of complex characters in _w_c_h_s_t_r, start‐
       ing at the current cursor position in  the  named  window.   Attributes
       (rendition) are stored with the characters.

       The  four  functions  with _n as the last argument return a leading sub‐
       string at most _n characters long  (exclusive  of  the  trailing  zeroed
       cccchhaarr__tt.   Transfer  stops  at  the  end of the current line, or when _n
       characters have been stored at the location referenced by _w_c_h_s_t_r.

       Constants defined in <<ccuurrsseess..hh>> can be used with the  &&  (logical  AND)
       operator to extract the character or the attribute alone from any posi‐
       tion in the _w_c_h_s_t_r [see ggeettcccchhaarr(3X)].

